 outside spending keep this competitive, but the weight of evidence favors McGuire by a modest margin.", "watch": "A second independent poll confirming a Perriello lead, or a major shift in the national environment, would move this toward Tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent John McGuire (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Virginia's 5th District leans Republican by about six points, and incumbent John McGuire is seeking a second term after surviving a contested primary. Tom Perriello, a well-known former congressman, has outraised McGuire and holds a large cash advantage, and national Democratic figures have campaigned alongside him in Charlottesville and Lynchburg.\n\nRecent polling shows a genuinely close race: a Washington Post/SSRS survey gives McGuire a 51-45 lead among likely voters, while a Democratic pollster's live survey found a one-point McGuire edge. Expert raters mostly call the race Lean or Likely Republican, and prediction markets price Perriello's chances around one in five. The race is competitive but tilts toward McGuire.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1914, "margin": -5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2771, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2238, "margin": -5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2476, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2003, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1957, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.2343, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.2412, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2798, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2488, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2134, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.3189, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.3108, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.2197, "margin": -4.0}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.2187, "margin": -4.0}]}